---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
	title="Contact and Participate | Bait Bikes"
	description="Start a Bait Bikes partnership or contribute to the public technology and education project."
	kicker="Contact"
>
	<header class="page-hero shell">
		<p class="eyebrow">Bring a real problem and the people who see it</p>
		<h1>Start a serious conversation about bicycle protection.</h1>
		<p class="lede">Bait Bikes is being built as a public-interest technology and education initiative. Agencies, cities, shops, campuses, manufacturers, riders, researchers, and civil-liberties reviewers all have useful knowledge to contribute.</p>
	</header>

	<section class="section light">
		<div class="shell">
			<div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Partnership inquiry</p><h2>Prepare five pieces of context.</h2></div><p>Do not include active-case details, live tracker links, personal data, credentials, or information that cannot be shared publicly in a GitHub issue.</p></div>
			<div class="card-grid">
				<article class="card"><span class="number">01</span><h3>Institution and geography</h3><p>Your role, organization type, jurisdiction or service area, and the partners already involved.</p></article>
				<article class="card"><span class="number">02</span><h3>Documented problem</h3><p>Available time range, broad theft pattern, reporting quality, public impact, and what is still unknown.</p></article>
				<article class="card"><span class="number">03</span><h3>Desired outcome</h3><p>Prevention, recovery, operation design, manufacturer integration, owner app, data contract, evaluation, or regional coordination.</p></article>
				<article class="card"><span class="number">04</span><h3>Safeguards</h3><p>Applicable legal or policy review, privacy needs, community concerns, evidence rules, and prohibited uses.</p></article>
				<article class="card"><span class="number">05</span><h3>Next step</h3><p>A bounded workshop, document review, pilot design, technical architecture session, or public contribution.</p></article>
				<article class="card"><span class="number">PUBLIC CHANNEL</span><h3>GitHub organization</h3><p>Use the public organization surface for source contributions and general project discussion. Private operational coordination will require a separately approved channel.</p></article>
			</div>
			<div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="https://github.com/bait-bikes">Visit Bait Bikes on GitHub</a><a class="button secondary" href="/partners/">Review the partnership model</a></div>
		</div>
	</section>
</SiteLayout>
